+	// Optimum (headless render harness): the channel order ReadDefaultFramebuffer
+	// leaves in the caller's buffer. The OpenGL path reads GL_BGRA, because that is
+	// what the screenshot path's SKBitmap wants. Every backend owes its callers the
+	// same order, so no platform overrides this: the Vulkan device's default colour
+	// target is R8G8B8A8_UNORM, and VulkanClientPlatform.ReadDefaultFramebuffer
+	// swaps red and blue on the way out rather than answering false here - answering
+	// false would fix the headless frames and leave the screenshot key and the AVI
+	// recorder swapped. The headless frame writer reads this so a backend that ever
+	// does hand back R G B A can say so.
